      "claim": "A PAMPA measurement for CP-409,092 indicates low passive permeability, but this is an artificial-membrane assay, not a direct F measurement, and the query differs in linker and lactam; it does not affirm F<20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C112"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "contradictory",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C112","C101","C117","C125"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct query-specific oral bioavailability or pharmacokinetic measurement is available.",
    "L3 exposure records lack intravenous comparators, so they cannot quantify absolute F.",
    "The L4 PAMPA value is for CP-409,092, not the query, and is not a direct intestinal absorption or systemic F measurement.",
    "Query neutral fraction at pH 7.4 is only 0.01; measured permeability, efflux, or first-pass data for the query are absent.",
    "Dose, formulation, and prandial state effects on the query are unknown.",
    "The two CP-409,092 solubility records (0.9 vs 25 mg/mL) are inconsistent and not resolved."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L4 adds a low PAMPA permeability signal for a close analog and adequate solubility records, but no affirmative F<20% evidence; direct L1 human F contexts and L3 oral exposure support F>=20%, so the high prediction is retained with moderate confidence."
}

